## Original Content
The 10-year U.S. Treasury yield fell and ING said the the long end of the Treasury curve will continue trading at higher yields even as Trump hasn’t delivered anything to shock markets so far.

## Summary
The yield on the 10-year U.S. Treasury bond fell, but ING bank predicts that yields at the longer end of the Treasury curve will remain elevated. This outlook persists despite President Trump not having introduced any market-shocking policies so far.

## Key Points
- 10-year U.S. Treasury yield decreased.
- ING forecasts long-end Treasury yields to continue rising.
- Trump has not delivered any market shocks yet.


